Author: vadvolo <volovikvd@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Aug 5 13:09:23 2026 +0000

    ssh: support legacy host-key/KEX/cipher algorithms for old devices
    
    Old network gear (FS/FSOS switches, aging RouterOS, etc.) only offers
    SHA-1 host keys (ssh-rsa/ssh-dss) and legacy KEX/ciphers, which Go's
    x/crypto/ssh disables by default. The handshake failed before auth, so
    the gnetcli server reported a generic connect_error.
    
    GetConfig now:
    - sets HostKeyAlgorithms explicitly, adding ssh-rsa and ssh-dss (modern
      algorithms kept first so strong devices still negotiate them);
    - keeps the legacy KEX (diffie-hellman-group-exchange-sha1,
      group1-sha1) and CBC/3DES cipher fallbacks.
    
    Verified against an FS S5810 (FSOS 11.4) that offers only ssh-rsa: the
    handshake now completes and "show version" returns cleanly via the fsos
    profile.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
